          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#IndConilpotency Ind-Conilpotency
          #IndConilpotency.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Pridham"}> Pridham 10, remark 3.15, remark 3.13
                )
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              an
              = succeed "-algebra," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-coalgebra"} dgc-coalgebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\bullet(\mathfrak{g})
              (
              %a{:href => "#ReformulationInSemifreeDgCoalgebra"}> above
              ) is
              = succeed "." do
                %em ind-conilpotent
            %p
              This means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\bullet(\mathfrak{g})
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              of sub-dg-coalgebras which are conilpotent, in that for each of them there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              such that their
              = succeed "-fold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "\u201D." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Artin+algebras"} local Artin algebras
            %p
              Moreover, since every dg-coalgebra is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
              of its finite-dimensonal subalgebras (see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebra"} dg-coalgebra
              the section
              = succeed ")," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "differential+graded+coalgebra#AsFilteredColimits"} As filtered colimits of finite-dimensional pieces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CE
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE_\bullet(\mathfrak{g})
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              of finite dimensional conilpotent coalgebras.
            %p
              This implies that the dual Chevalley-Eilenberg cochain algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi CE
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE^\bullet(\mathfrak{g})
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+limit"} filtered limit
              of finite-dimensional nilpotent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebras"} dgc-algebras
              (actual
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Artin+algebras"} local Artin algebras
          %h3#model_category_structure Model category structure
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} model structure for L-∞ algebras
          %h3#relation_to_dglie_algebras Relation to dg-Lie algebras
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            is in an evident way an
            = succeed "-algebra." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 2
            are trivial. These may be thought of as the
            %em strict
            = succeed "-algebras:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            holds on the nose and all its possible higher coherences are trivial.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              0 and write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty Alg_k
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\infty
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %p
              Then every object of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty Alg_k
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
              to a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
            %p
              Moreover, one can find a functorial replacement: there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W : L_\infty Alg_k \to L_\infty Alg_k
            %p
              such that for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} \in L_\infty Alg_k
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔨
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{k})
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebra"} dg-Lie algebra
              %li
                %p
                  there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mo ≃
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\mathfrak{g} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                        W(\mathfrak{g})
                        \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#KrizMay95"}> Kriz &amp; May 1995, Cor. 1.6
            ).
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras+and+dg-Lie+algebras"} relation between L-∞ algebras and dg-Lie algebras
          %h3#relation_to_lie_groupoids
            Relation to
            = succeed "-Lie" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            In generalization to how a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            integrates to a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Lie+group"} ∞-Lie group
          %p See
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
          %p and
          %p
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie+infinity-groupoid#LieIntegrated"}> Lie integrated ∞-Lie groupoids
            \.
