                    %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.12517"}> arXiv:2312.12517
                    ]
            %h4#ReferencesBVBRSTFormalism In BV-BRST formalism
            %p
              The introduction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complexes"} BV-BRST complexes
              as a model for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"} action functionals
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
              is due to
            %ul
              %li#BatalinVilkovisky81
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Batalin"}> Igor Batalin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigori+Vilkovisky"} Grigori Vilkovisky
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Gauge Algebra and Quantization
              %li#BatalinVilkovisky83
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Batalin"}> Igor Batalin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigori+Vilkovisky"} Grigori Vilkovisky
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Feynman rules for reducible gauge theories
                %p doi:10.1016/0370-2693(83)90645-7
              %li#BatakinFradkin83
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Batalin"}> Igor Batalin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Efim+Fradkin"} Efim Fradkin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em A generalized canonical formalism and quantization of reducible gauge theories
              %li#BatalinVilkovisky83b
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Batalin"}> Igor Batalin
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grigori+Vilkovisky"} Grigori Vilkovisky
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Quantization of Gauge Theories with Linearly Dependent Generators
            %p as reviewed in
            %ul
              %li#HenneauxTeitelboim92
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Henneaux"}> Marc Henneaux
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Teitelboim"} Claudio Teitelboim
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quantization+of+Gauge+Systems"} Quantization of Gauge Systems
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joaquim+Gomis"}> Joaquim Gomis
                  , J. Paris, S. Samuel,
                  %em Antibrackets, Antifields and Gauge Theory Quantization
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9412228"}> arXiv:hep-th/9412228
                  )
            %p
              The understanding that these
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complexes"} BV-BRST complexes
              mathematically are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+L-%E2%88%9E+algebroid"} derived L-∞ algebroid
              originates around
            %ul
              %li#Stasheff96
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Homological Reduction of Constrained Poisson Algebras
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9603021"} arXiv:q-alg/9603021
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214459757"} Euclid
              %li#Stasheff97
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
                  ,
                  %em The (secret?) homological algebra of the Batalin-Vilkovisky approach
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9712157"}> arXiv:hep-th/9712157
                  )
            %p
              Discussion in terms of homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Rinehart+pairs"} Lie-Rinehart pairs
              is due to
            %ul
              %li#Kjeseth01
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lars+Kjeseth"}> Lars Kjeseth
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy Rinehart cohomology of homotopy Lie-Rinehart pairs
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.hha/1140370269"} Euclid
            %p
              The
              = succeed "-structure" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebroid"} L-∞ algebroid
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4001v1"} def. 4.1 of v1
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiberStasheff09"} Sati-Schreiber-Stasheff 09
            %p
              The extraction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebras
              from the formal neighbourhood of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
              is maybe first made explicit in:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Grigoriev"}> Maxim Grigoriev
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Rudinsky"} Dmitry Rudinsky
                %em
                  Notes on the
                  = succeed "-approach" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.08990"} arXiv2303.08990
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %h4#in_string_field_theory In string field theory
            %p
              The first
              %em explicit
              appearance of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string"} closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
              found in the context of closed bosonic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
              in
            %ul
              %li#Zwiebach92
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"}> Barton Zwiebach
                  ,
                  %em Closed string field theory: Quantum action and the B-V master equation
                  , Nucl.Phys. B390 (1993) 33 (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9206084"}> arXiv:hep-th/9206084
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
                  ,
                  %em Closed string field theory, strong homotopy Lie algebras and the operad actions of moduli space
                  Talk given at the
                  %em Conference on Topics in Geometry and Physics
                  (1992) (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9304061"}> arXiv:hep-th/9304061
                  )
            %p
              Generalization to open-closed bosonic string field theory yields
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              interacting with
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} A-∞ algebra
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshige+Kajiura"}> Hiroshige Kajiura
                  ,
                  %em Homotopy Algebra Morphism and Geometry of Classical String Field Theory
                  (2001) (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0112228"}> arXiv:hep-th/0112228
                  )
              %li#KajiuraStasheff04
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hiroshige+Kajiura"}> Hiroshige Kajiura
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Homotopy algebras inspired by classical open-closed string field theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0410291"} arXiv:math/0410291
              %li#Markl
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Markl"}> Martin Markl
                  ,
                  %em Loop Homotopy Algebras in Closed String Field Theory
                  (1997) (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711045"}> arXiv:hep-th/9711045
                  )
            %p See also
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Higher homotopy algebras: String field theory and Drinfeld’s quasiHopf algebras
                = succeed "," do
                  %em International Conference on Differential Geometric Methods in Theoretical Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/record/327712"} spire
            %p
              For more see at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "string%20field%20theory#ReferencesHomotopyAlgebra"} string field theory – References – Relation to A-infinity and L-infinity algebras
            %h4#in_deformation_quantization In deformation quantization
            %p
              The general solution of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
              problem of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
              due to
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#Kontsevich97"} Kontsevich 97
            %p
              makes crucial use of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              are equivalently the universal model for infinitesimal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
              (of anything), also called
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+moduli+problems"} formal moduli problems
            %ul
              %li#Hinich98
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
                  ,
                  %em DG coalgebras as formal stacks
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9812034"}> arXiv:9812034
                  )
              %li#Lurie
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                  ,
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Formal+Moduli+Problems"} Formal Moduli Problems
              %li#Pridham
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Pridham"}> Jonathan Pridham
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Unifying derived deformation theories
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.0344"} arXiv:0705.0344
            %h4#in_heterotic_string_theory In heterotic string theory
            %p
              Next it was again
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              that drew attention. It was eventually understood that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structures"} string structures
              which embody a refinement of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly+cancellation"} Green-Schwarz anomaly cancellation
              mechanism in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
              have a further smooth refinement as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structures"} G-structures
              for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+2-algebra"} Lie 2-algebra
              called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+Lie+2-algebra"} string Lie 2-algebra
            %ul
              %li#BCSS
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alissa+Crans"} Alissa Crans
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em From loop groups to 2-groups
                  %em Homotopy, Homology and Applications
                  %strong 9
                  (2007), 101-135. (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.QA/0504123"}> arXiv:math.QA/0504123
                  )
              %li#Henriques
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      Integrating
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                      algebras
                  %strong 144
                  (2008), no. 4, 1017–1045 (
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1112/S0010437X07003405"}> doi
                  ,
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0603563"}> math.AT/0603563
                  )
            %p and the relation to the Green-Schwarz mechanism is made explicit in
            %ul
              %li#SatiSchreiberStasheff09
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Twisted+Differential+String+and+Fivebrane+Structures"} Twisted Differential String and Fivebrane Structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.4001"} arXiv:0910.4001
            %p
              This article also observes that an analogous situation appears in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+heterotic+string+theory"} dual heterotic string theory
              with the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fivebrane+Lie+6-algebra"} fivebrane Lie 6-algebra
              in place of the string Lie 2-algebra.
            %h4#higher_chernsimons_field_theory_and_aksz_sigmamodels Higher Chern-Simons field theory and AKSZ sigma-models
            %p
              Ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
              for a simple gauge group is all controled by a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra 3-cocycle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ-sigma+models"} AKSZ-sigma models
              was understood to be encoded by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+Lie+n-algebroids"} symplectic Lie n-algebroids
              (later re-popularized as “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+symplectic+structures"}> shifted symplectic structures
              ”) in
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
                  ,
                  %em Courant algebroids, derived brackets and even symplectic supermanifolds
                  PhD thesis (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9910078"}> arXiv:9910078
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavol+%C5%A0evera"}> Pavol Ševera
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Some+title+containing+the+words+%22homotopy%22+and+%22symplectic%22%2C+e.g.+this+one"} Some title containing the words "homotopy" and "symplectic", e.g. this one
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0105080"} arXiv:0105080
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
                  ,
                  %em On the structure of graded symplectic supermanifolds and Courant algebroids
                  in
                  %em Quantization, Poisson Brackets and Beyond
                  ,
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Voronov"} Theodore Voronov
                  (ed.), Contemp. Math., Vol. 315, Amer. Math. Soc., Providence, RI, 2002 (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0203110"}> arXiv
                  )
              %li#Roytenberg
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitry+Roytenberg"}> Dmitry Roytenberg
                  ,
                  %em AKSZ-BV Formalism and Courant Algebroid-induced Topological Field Theories
                  Lett.Math.Phys.79:143-159,2007 (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0608150"}> arXiv:hep-th/0608150
                  ).
            %p The globally defined AKSZ action functionals obtained this way were shown in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/AKSZ+Sigma-Models+in+Higher+Chern-Weil+Theory"} AKSZ Sigma-Models in Higher Chern-Weil Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.4378"} arXiv:1108.4378
            %p to be a special case of the higher Lie integration process of
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+cocycles+for+differential+characteristic+classes"} Cech cocycles for differential characteristic classes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.4735"} arXiv:1011.4735
            %p
              Further exmaples of non-symplectic
              = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
              on
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} string 2-connections
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/7d+Chern-Simons+theory+and+the+5-brane"} Multiple M5-branes, String 2-connections, and 7d nonabelian Chern-Simons theory
            %h4#in_local_prequantum_field_theory In local prequantum field theory
            %p
              Infinite-dimensional
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
              –
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket+Lie+n-algebras"} Poisson bracket Lie n-algebras
              – were noticed
            %ul
              %li#Rogers10
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                  ,
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                    algebras from multisymplectic geometry
                  , Letters in Mathematical Physics April 2012, Volume 100, Issue 1, pp 29-50 (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1005.2230"}> arXiv:1005.2230
                  ,
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a{:href => "http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007%2Fs11005-011-0493-x"} journal
              %li#Rogers11
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"}> Chris Rogers
                  ,
                  %em Higher symplectic geometry
                  PhD thesis (2011) (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4068"}> arXiv:1106.4068
                  )
            %p In
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras+of+local+observables+from+higher+prequantum+bundles"} L-∞ algebras of local observables from higher prequantum bundles
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.6292"} arXiv:1304.6292
            %p
              these were shown to be the infinitesimal version of the symmetries of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+n-bundles"} prequantum n-bundles
              as they appear in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket"} Poisson bracket
              is the Lie algebra of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantomorphism+group"} quantomorphism group
            %p
              These also encode a homotopy refinement of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickey+bracket"} Dickey bracket
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noether+theorem"} Noether
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
              which for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+sigma+models"} Green-Schwarz sigma models
              reduces to Lie
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+charges"} BPS charges
              which refine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
              such as the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+super+Lie+algebra"} M-theory super Lie algebra
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Lie+n-algebras+of+BPS+charges"} Lie n-algebras of BPS charges
                  (
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1507.08692"}> arXiv:1507.08692
                  )
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Khavkine"}> Igor Khavkine
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Lie+n-algebras+of+higher+Noether+currents"} Lie n-algebras of higher Noether currents
            %p
              This makes concrete the suggestion that there should be
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dickey+bracket"} Dickey bracket
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field+theory"} local field theory
              that was made in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glenn+Barnich"}> Glenn Barnich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ronald+Fulp"} Ronald Fulp
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Lada"} Tom Lada
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                %em The sh Lie structure of Poisson brackets in field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702176"}> arXiv:hep-th/9702176
                )
            %p Comprehesive survey and exposition of this situation is in
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Prequantum+Geometry"} Higher Prequantum Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel+Catren"} Gabriel Catren
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathieu+Anel"} Mathieu Anel
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/New+Spaces+for+Mathematics+and+Physics"} New Spaces for Mathematics and Physics
            %h4#in_perturbative_quantum_field_theory In perturbative quantum field theory
            %p
              Further identification of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              in the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+amplitudes"} Feynman amplitudes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-matrix"} S-matrix
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative quantum field theory
            %ul
              %li#Froeb18
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markus+Fr%C3%B6b"}> Markus Fröb
                  ,
                  %em Anomalies in time-ordered products and applications to the BV-BRST formulation of quantum gauge theories
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s00220-019-03558-6"} Communications in Mathematical Physics
                  2019 (online first) (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1803.10235"}> arXiv:1803.10235
                  )
              %li#Arvanitakis19
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alex+Arvanitakis"}> Alex Arvanitakis
                  ,
                  %em
                    The
                    = succeed "-algebra" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.05643"}> arXiv:1903.05643
                  )
            %h4#in_double_field_theory In double field theory
            %p
              In
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+field+theory"} double field theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Deser"}> Andreas Deser
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Even symplectic supermanifolds and double field theory
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1406.3601"} arXiv:1406.3601
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Olaf+Hohm"}> Olaf Hohm
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barton+Zwiebach"} Barton Zwiebach
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                    Algebras and Field Theory
                  (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1701.08824"}> arXiv:1701.08824
                  )
            %h3#related_expositions Related expositions
            %ul
              %li
